1
00:00:03,666 --> 00:00:10,686
Here's our table, units already
set. Let's give it real materials.

2
00:00:10,736 --> 00:00:31,516
On the Materials tab, New Wood
opens a procedural wood material.

3
00:00:31,566 --> 00:00:40,511
The editor previews the material as you
adjust it. Save adds it to the project.

4
00:00:40,561 --> 00:00:47,661
Select the table top, then choose Apply Material.

5
00:00:47,711 --> 00:01:03,885
Ooh, look at that grain! Materials belong
to each instance, so select all four legs.

6
00:01:03,935 --> 00:01:13,952
Nice. For the ground, snap a
large rectangle around the table.

7
00:01:14,002 --> 00:01:18,927
New Grass grows real blades on
whatever surface it's applied to.

8
00:01:18,977 --> 00:01:32,727
Set the blade height and density here, then Save.

9
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:42,830
Wooow, real grass! Materials are saved
with the project, editable at any time.
